{
  "site": "../examples/tallyboard",
  "agent": "claude",
  "keep": 2,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "cold",
      "montage": true,
      "hold": 7000,
      "step": "Variantly",
      "kinetic": {
        "text": "Four redesigns. One command.",
        "sub": "npx variantly",
        "from": 3.6
      },
      "text": "",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "hi",
      "chapter": {
        "n": 1,
        "title": "Hi"
      },
      "step": "Hi",
      "lower": {
        "name": "Joaquin",
        "role": "Variantly"
      },
      "text": "Hi, I'm Joaquin from Variantly. This is Tallyboard. It works. It just looks like every other template on the internet, and redesigning it means picking one direction and hoping it was the right one. Variantly takes a different approach. Your own coding agent redesigns your whole site several times over, each in a different direction. Every redesign runs as your real site, side by side. You keep the one you like.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "goto": "{{site}}"
        },
        {
          "wait": 3000
        },
        {
          "scroll": 900,
          "ms": 3200
        },
        {
          "wait": 2500
        },
        {
          "scroll": 2000,
          "ms": 3000
        },
        {
          "wait": 2000
        },
        {
          "scroll": 0,
          "ms": 2500
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "promise",
      "step": "Hi",
      "hold": 2800,
      "kinetic": {
        "text": "Nothing changes until you keep one."
      },
      "text": "",
      "actions": [
        {
          "wait": 300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "need",
      "chapter": {
        "n": 2,
        "title": "What you need"
      },
      "step": "What you need",
      "terminal": {
        "lines": [
          "$ node -v",
          "v22.18.0",
          "$ claude --version",
          "Claude Code",
          "$ npx variantly"
        ]
      },
      "lower": {
        "name": "Designs by Impeccable",
        "role": "impeccable.style",
        "from": 14
      },
      "text": "You need two things: Node, and Claude Code signed in. Codex and Copilot work too. In your project, run npx variantly. It opens a wizard in your browser. The design work itself is done by Impeccable, an open-source design skill for coding agents. If your agent doesn't have it yet, Variantly installs it for you in one click.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "wait": 5500
        },
        {
          "goto": "{{app}}"
        },
        {
          "waitFor": "#wiz-title"
        },
        {
          "wait": 1500
        },
        {
          "realOnly": true,
          "click": "role=button[name=\"Install Impeccable\"]",
          "zoom": true,
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "realOnly": true,
          "waitFor": "text=/Claude Code ready/",
          "timeoutMs": 240000,
          "optional": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "setup",
      "chapter": {
        "n": 3,
        "title": "Setup"
      },
      "step": "Setup",
      "text": "Setup finds your app and how to run it, checks your agent and Impeccable, and tells you anything that would get in the way. Each variant will run your dev command on its own port. By default the agent may only edit files, inside its own copy of your project.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "spotlight": "text=/app found/",
          "ms": 1950,
          "point": true
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=/ ready/",
          "ms": 1650,
          "point": true
        },
        {
          "click": "text=Use a different app or agent"
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=Dev command",
          "ms": 1800,
          "pad": 60
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=Permissions",
          "ms": 1800,
          "pad": 40,
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "click": "text=Use a different app or agent"
        },
        {
          "click": "role=button[name=/^Continue to variants$/]",
          "zoom": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "make",
      "chapter": {
        "n": 4,
        "title": "What to make"
      },
      "step": "What to make",
      "text": "Pick how many variants: two, four or six. We'll take four, for the home page. Extras are optional Impeccable passes: sharper copy, motion, small moments of delight, a phone pass, or hardening for accessibility. Under more settings, Redesign gives every variant a different visual world, and Refine keeps your look and improves it. Leave a direction blank and Impeccable chooses one, or type your own. Two agents work at a time. Each one gets a real browser to check its own work, then a review pass critiques and fixes it, and everything is scored with axe-core and Lighthouse, on your machine.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "click": "role=radio[name=\"4\"]",
          "zoom": true
        },
        {
          "wait": 800
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=Which pages?",
          "ms": 1800,
          "pad": 40
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "label.pick:has-text(\"Rewrite the copy\")",
          "ms": 1500,
          "callout": "Sharper headlines, buttons and labels. Facts, prices and names stay.",
          "point": true
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "label.pick:has-text(\"Add motion\")",
          "ms": 1500,
          "callout": "Purposeful transitions and entrances, with reduced motion respected.",
          "point": true
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "label.pick:has-text(\"Add delight\")",
          "ms": 1500,
          "callout": "Small moments of personality: empty states, hovers, details.",
          "point": true
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "label.pick:has-text(\"Polish for phones\")",
          "ms": 1500,
          "callout": "Check every chosen page at phone width and fix what breaks.",
          "point": true
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "label.pick:has-text(\"Harden\")",
          "ms": 1500,
          "callout": "Accessibility, focus states, long text and error states.",
          "point": true
        },
        {
          "click": "text=More settings"
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=Approach",
          "ms": 3200,
          "pad": 50
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=/Your own directions/",
          "ms": 3000,
          "pad": 60
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=At a time",
          "ms": 1800,
          "pad": 30
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=Around Impeccable",
          "ms": 5200,
          "pad": 90
        },
        {
          "click": "text=More settings"
        },
        {
          "click": "role=button[name=\"Continue to your site\"]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "site",
      "chapter": {
        "n": 5,
        "title": "About your site"
      },
      "step": "About your site",
      "text": "Then a few words about your site: who it's for, what it offers, and, most importantly, what must stay. Here: the prices, the sign-up button and the FAQ. Agents change presentation, never behaviour: every page, form and piece of copy stays.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "fill": "role=textbox[name=/Who is it for/]",
          "text": "Small agencies that bill by the hour.",
          "delay": 30
        },
        {
          "fill": "role=textbox[name=/What does it offer/]",
          "text": "Timers, timesheets and invoices.",
          "delay": 30
        },
        {
          "fill": "role=textbox[name=/What must stay/]",
          "text": "Prices, the sign-up button, the FAQ.",
          "delay": 30
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "role=textbox[name=/What must stay/]",
          "ms": 3500,
          "pad": 30
        },
        {
          "click": "role=button[name=\"Continue to review\"]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "review",
      "chapter": {
        "n": 6,
        "title": "Review"
      },
      "step": "Review",
      "text": "The review shows exactly what will run, and how many agent sessions it uses on your own account. Make four variants.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "wait": 800
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "text=/Uses \\d+ sessions|Nothing is spent/",
          "ms": 4000,
          "pad": 20
        },
        {
          "click": "role=button[name=/^Make \\d+ variants?$/]",
          "zoom": true,
          "sound": "whoosh"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "worktrees",
      "chapter": {
        "n": 7,
        "title": "The run"
      },
      "step": "The run",
      "diagram": "worktrees",
      "text": "Each variant gets its own git worktree, outside your project, and its own dev server. Your checkout isn't touched.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "waitFor": "body[data-view=\"board\"]"
        },
        {
          "wait": 500
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "board",
      "step": "The run",
      "text": "The board shows every variant live: its direction, status, the files it changed, and what it's using on your account as it goes.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "spotlight": "role=columnheader[name=\"Direction\"]",
          "ms": 1800,
          "pad": 30
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "role=columnheader[name=\"Status\"]",
          "ms": 1500,
          "pad": 30
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "role=columnheader[name=\"Files\"]",
          "ms": 1500,
          "pad": 30
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "role=columnheader[name=\"Usage\"]",
          "ms": 1800,
          "pad": 30
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent",
      "step": "The run",
      "text": "Here's one agent at work. It reads your site, lets Impeccable choose a direction, and builds it. Then it opens its variant in a real browser, at desktop and phone width, and fixes what it sees. A second session reviews the result with Impeccable's critique and audit, and fixes the worst problems without changing the direction. If a variant goes wrong, stop it or retry it on its own. The others keep going.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "click": "role=button[name=\"Show V01 output\"]"
        },
        {
          "wait": 14000
        },
        {
          "spotlight": "role=button[name=\"Stop\"]",
          "ms": 3000,
          "pad": 20,
          "point": true,
          "optional": true
        }
      ]
    },
